building machines of war in what used to  be a shoe factory just two months ago  Artyom Dima and Maxine made Footwear in  this Kiev workshop then they switched to  munitions Artyom used 3d computer models  to develop these mounting brackets for  Kalashnikovs the boys at the front and  with these brackets for various  applications but especially to attach a  scope we've designed several versions  even for grenade launchers these are not  toys they're made for war the men don't  build actual weapons here but the parts  they make are vital for weapon precision  this order is bound for the front just  how many parts are inside the shipment  is a secret a few kilometers away we  visit a warehouse on the city's edge  this is where Kalashnikov brackets and  various other goods come before they're  distributed to soldiers anna is a  coordinator here every three days she  says someone from the front comes to  pick up supplies bags boots warm  underwear helmets bulletproof vests and  packages with food and medicine items  that should be supplied by the  government but instead are financed by  donations both from Ukraine and abroad  sometimes the goods are old and  substandard the volunteers say these do  more harm than good I feel guilty about  the soldiers who have died or are dying  because of bad provisions the ones were  fighting and depending on our help in  the meantime we've had to borrow so much  money that some of us are close to  bankruptcy but people keep helping us  around town it's now common to see  people out collecting money for  Ukraine's army an army that critics say  could hardly win a war because it's  fighting with equipment that dates as  far back as World War two  that's exactly the problem facing the  Ukrainian forces quality Gansa that  don't shoot straight bulletproof vests  that are Abdullah proof and uniforms  that are not warm enough for winter  conditions
 

